            "title": "The One Bottle Nipple Feature Most Parents Never Think About",
            "body": "<p>Hosfu wasn’t created by simply adding <strong>another vent to a traditional bottle design</strong>.</p><p>Its team tested dozens of <strong>nipple shapes, widths, angles, and flow rates</strong> to find the combination that helped babies maintain a more stable latch—not just the one that looked most like a breast in product photos.</p><p>The final nipple uses <strong>platinum-cured silicone</strong>, a <strong>wider base</strong>, and a <strong>15-degree natural feeding angle</strong> to sit more comfortably in the way a baby’s mouth naturally meets the breast.</p><p>That angle makes a real difference.</p><p>Instead of a long, straight nipple pressing awkwardly into the mouth, Moka helps babies <strong>draw the nipple in, seal around the base, and stay in rhythm</strong> without repeatedly slipping off.</p><p>Its <strong>five flow stages</strong> are designed to support that latch rather than work against it.</p><p>Babies get a feeding pace suited to their stage, while the nipple shape helps them <strong>latch more deeply and feed more naturally</strong>.</p>"
