            "body": "<p>Moka is a <strong>premium, limited-run bottle</strong>—not another “anti-colic” option relying on clever marketing.</p><p>Where milk makes contact, Moka uses <strong>borosilicate glass, heat-resistant PPSU, and platinum-cured silicone</strong> instead of low-cost plastic that becomes harder to trust after repeated sterilization.</p><p>That matters because baby bottles go through a lot.</p><p>They are <strong>boiled, steamed, washed, dropped, reheated, packed, and handled half-asleep at 3 a.m.</strong></p><p>Cheaper materials often show the strain. They can <strong>warp, scratch, turn cloudy, absorb odors, and begin to leak</strong> before eventually being pushed to the back of the cupboard.</p><p>Hosfu was designed for <strong>real daily use</strong>, not simply to look good on a store shelf.</p>"
